{"availability":"available","full":"semnil/urx-router","name":"urx-router","description":"Routing planner & unofficial mixer control (read / write / live sync) for the YAMAHA URX22 / URX44 / URX44V USB audio interfaces","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":4,"forks":1,"created":"2026-06-15T00:41:21Z","updated":"2026-10-11T02:06:41Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://urx-router.semnil.com","topics":["audio-interface","audio-routing","mixer-control","tauri","typescript","urx","urx22","urx44","urx44v","usb-audio","yamaha"],"demo":"https://urx-router.semnil.com/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:30.056Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:30.056Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:30.056Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T02:10:30.056Z","stars":4,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A routing planner and unofficial mixer controller (read / write / live sync) for the YAMAHA URX22 / URX44 / URX44V USB audio interfaces.","Based on the official block diagram, it visualizes input/output channels, mixer buses, and output patches as boxes and wires, and constrains the GUI so that only physically routable paths can be wired. Plans are saved/loaded as JSON, and the diagram can be exported as an image.","The URX series has no dspMixFx-style mixer editor — dspMixFx supports the UR-C / URX-C lines, not the URX22 / URX44 / URX44V. Out of the box, the full mixer is only editable on the unit's touch screen: the official Stream Deck plugin covers one-touch operations like level steps, mutes, and processing-block on/off toggles, and the Cubase / Nuendo / MixKey integration screens work only while that software is running. URX Router fills this gap: it reads, writes, and live-syncs the entire mixer from your computer, with or without a DAW — see Device control."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/semnil/urx-router/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"08b459176f099e5e